WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.770
So, you've already binged The Mandalorian.

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:03.770
Now what?

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.000
If you're still wondering whether or not to
stick by the House of Mouse, we've got you

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.000
covered.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.670
Here's your comprehensive rundown of all the
exciting original shows and movies being produced

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.969
exclusively for Disney+ in 2020.

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:15.280
The Mandalorian: Season 2

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.299
This is the big one.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:20.520
The Mandalorian and Baby Yoda stormed the
internet when Disney+ launched in November

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.750
of 2019, and the show seemed to hit that sweet
spot of mainstream success and obsessive fandom

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.220
that made it a must watch.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.140
A second season of the show was obvious - what's
surprising is how quickly we'll be able to

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.500
sit down and watch it.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.460
As soon as the season finale debuted in December,
showrunner Jon Favreau revealed that the second

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.739
season of The Mandalorian is slated to arrive
in fall 2020.

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:45.780
The show debuted on November 12, 2019, so
the follow-up arriving a year later seems

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.249
like a pretty good bet.

00:00:47.249 --> 00:00:51.140
There were quite a few cliffhangers left over
at the end of The Mandalorian's first season.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:55.350
We and the characters don't know much real
information about Baby Yoda, and all signs

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.929
point to the second season focusing on the
search for the child's home.

00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:02.690
There's also still the threat of Moff Gideon
- and his Darksaber - to deal with.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:03.690
WandaVision

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:08.140
One of the two original MCU shows coming to
Disney+ in 2020, WandaVision looks to be a

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.610
bit of a strange one.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:14.880
The series focuses on Wanda Maximoff a.k.a.
Scarlet Witch, and her late android lover

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.790
Vision, who up until now was maybe the deadest
character in the entire MCU.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:23.210
As for how he's back, or what they'll be up
to, that's anyone's guess.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.630
So far, the imagery we've seen from WandaVision
evokes a particularly strange Leave it to

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:28.630
Beaver vibe.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:33.220
Paul Bettany reportedly told an audience at
the D23 expo that the show would have old

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:37.530
school sitcom vibes with some serious darkness
hidden just below the surface.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:42.260
Some familiar faces from the MCU will appear
along the way, including Darcy Lewis, Jimmy

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.700
Woo, and an all-grown-up Monica Rambeau, now
played by Teyonah Parris.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.280
We're intrigued to see what will bring them
all together.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.100
Considering where the MCU appears to be headed
with some of its post-Infinity Saga releases,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.920
it's been theorized that WandaVision will
serve as a way to introduce supernatural and

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.330
horror elements into the greater MCU.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:04.820
Guardians of the Galaxy did something similar
with cosmic concepts on its original release,

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.860
and Doctor Strange opened the door for mysticism
to find its way into the franchise.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:12.459
It'll be interesting to see what types of
risks Marvel and Disney take with Wanda's

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:14.349
reality-bending powers post-Endgame.

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:18.069
"I don't even know who you are."

00:02:18.069 --> 00:02:19.069
"You will."

00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:20.069
Falcon and the Winter Soldier

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:24.260
The second MCU show hitting Disney+ this year
is Falcon and the Winter Soldier.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:27.819
We've got a few details on this one, but the
showrunners have generally played it pretty

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:29.129
close to the chest.

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:33.239
Anthony Mackie and Sebastian Stan will be
reprising their title roles, and a lot of

00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:35.160
the other cast has been revealed as well.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.909
Daniel Bruhl is returning as Captain America:
Civil War’s Helmut Zemo.

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:41.819
Emily VanCamp will reprise her role as Sharon
Carter.

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:46.560
Wyatt Russell, meanwhile, joins the cast as
John Walker, a.k.a. U.S. Agent.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.409
Falcon and the Winter Soldier is slated to
consist of six episodes that will release

00:02:50.409 --> 00:02:54.810
weekly, rather than all at once - a strategy
Disney+ seems to be favoring for all of its

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.069
original series.

00:02:56.069 --> 00:02:59.959
With director Kari Skogland at the helm for
every episode, the show looks to follow in

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:03.170
the vein of the Captain America films, playing
like a spy thriller.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:07.209
It will focus on Sam Wilson adapting to his
role as the new Captain America following

00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:09.689
the events of Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:10.689
Star Wars: The Clone Wars Season 7

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:13.319
Star Wars: The Clone Wars, set during the
time between Attack of the Clones and Revenge

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:17.849
of the Sith, originally debuted in 2008 as
a feature film that served as a pilot for

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:19.189
the animated series.

00:03:19.189 --> 00:03:24.040
The show then ran for five seasons on Cartoon
Network before being cancelled, with 13 leftover

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.569
episodes eventually hitting Netflix as a makeshift
sixth season.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:31.450
But there were still scripts left unproduced
and plot threads left dangling.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:35.540
Fans kept hope alive, and their campaigning
was finally rewarded when a definitive seventh

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.040
and final season was announced for Disney+.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:43.010
A trailer released in January 2020 teased
the revival's thrilling return to the storylines

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:47.549
fans have been waiting to see concluded for
years - the romance of Anakin and Padme, the

00:03:47.549 --> 00:03:51.989
moral struggle of the clone soldiers, and
a climactic showdown between Ahsoka Tano and

00:03:51.989 --> 00:03:53.060
Darth Maul.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:57.709
It's a miracle revival that fans have been
waiting for; the wait finally ends on February

00:03:57.709 --> 00:03:58.709
21st.

00:03:58.709 --> 00:03:59.709
Muppets Now

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:03.910
The Muppets are coming to Disney+ in 2020,
but not in the format you might expect.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:08.219
Muppets Now will feature celebrity guests
and is being touted as an unscripted series,

00:04:08.219 --> 00:04:11.069
but there aren't a ton of details available
outside of that.

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:15.109
The promise of celebrity guests suggests that
the project could resemble the original Muppet

00:04:15.109 --> 00:04:19.989
Show variety series from the 1970s, but we'll
have to wait for more details to learn more.

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:25.610
The Muppets last had a show on ABC in 2015,
following a pair of feature films in 2011

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.830
and 2014.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.770
These iterations were largely dedicated to
playing on the nostalgia of adults who grew

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.229
up with the characters.

00:04:32.229 --> 00:04:36.280
Time will tell if Muppets Now represents a
fresh retooling for a streaming audience,

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:39.320
but regardless, it will be a welcome return
to the spotlight.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.830
The Phineas and Ferb Movie: Candace Against
the Universe

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.139
Phineas and Ferb, a cartoon series that ran
from 2007 through 2015, is the story of two

00:04:45.139 --> 00:04:50.460
brothers who are constantly inventing extraordinary
ways to pass time during their summer vacation.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:53.710
Their sister, Candace, is always trying to
get them in trouble, and their pet platypus

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:59.370
moonlights as a James Bond-esque spy, constantly
thwarting the villainous plans of Dr. Doofenshmirtz.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.430
Pretty standard stuff.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:04.560
The original creators are returning for a
feature film called The Phineas and Ferb Movie:

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.990
Candace Against the Universe.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:10.550
According to Disney's official announcement
at D23 in 2019, the plot will feature the

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.810
two brothers traveling across the galaxy to
rescue their sister.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:17.580
The Phineas and Ferb Movie: Candace Against
the Universe will reportedly release in the

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.100
summer of 2020, though an official date has
yet to be announced.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.100
Lizzie McGuire

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:25.300
While there have been some behind-the-scenes
shake-ups during production, as far as we

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.949
know, we can still expect a full season of
the Lizzie McGuire reboot in 2020.

00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:30.949
"Hi!

00:05:30.949 --> 00:05:31.949
It's me."

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:35.550
Hilary Duff is confirmed to return in the
title role, with much of her supporting cast

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:37.370
expected to be on board as well.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:41.699
The new Lizzie McGuire was set to kick off
with Lizzie's 30th birthday in New York City,

00:05:41.699 --> 00:05:44.819
where she would be seen working as an interior
design apprentice.

00:05:44.819 --> 00:05:49.650
However, Variety reports that show creator
Terri Minsky parted ways with the reboot after

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.300
only two episodes were filmed.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.860
According to a Disney spokesperson,

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:56.610
"After filming two episodes, we concluded
that we need to move in a different creative

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:59.240
direction and are putting a new lens on the
show."

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:03.509
The show was supposed to release this year,
and possibly still will - we just don't have

00:06:03.509 --> 00:06:04.629
further details yet.

00:06:04.629 --> 00:06:05.629
Monsters at Work

00:06:05.629 --> 00:06:08.140
Get some more Pixar in your life with Monsters
at Work.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:12.389
This series is a direct sequel to Monsters,
Inc., picking up six months after the 2001

00:06:12.389 --> 00:06:13.389
film.

00:06:13.389 --> 00:06:17.909
It will introduce a new character, Tylor Tuskmon,
who graduates as the top scarer in his college

00:06:17.909 --> 00:06:18.909
class.

00:06:18.909 --> 00:06:22.210
He comes to work at Monsters, Inc. on the
day the company switches over from scares

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:24.780
to laughter, leaving him unsure how to move
forward.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.990
Much of the Monsters movies' all-star cast,
including John Goodman and Billy Crystal,

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:33.060
will reunite for the series, with Tylor being
played by Ben Feldman, known for his work

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:35.500
on Mad Men, Silicon Valley, and more.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.780
"I just wanna be a part of this place.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.889
I think it's on the way up."

00:06:39.889 --> 00:06:43.860
There's no official release date yet for Monsters
at Work, but Disney has announced that we

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:44.960
can expect it this year.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:45.960
Chip 'n' Dale

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:50.831
You might remember these two cartoon chipmunks
from the 1989-90 Rescue Rangers cartoon, but

00:06:50.831 --> 00:06:53.300
Chip and Dale have been around much longer
than that.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:57.189
They originally appeared as troublemakers
in classic Disney animated shorts starting

00:06:57.189 --> 00:07:01.130
in the 1940s, frequently antagonizing Donald
Duck or Pluto.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:05.289
Disney+ has plans for the chipmunk duo, and
is rebooting Chip 'n' Dale in that classic

00:07:05.289 --> 00:07:06.680
cartoon philosophy.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:11.379
The new cartoon will be comprised of 39 short
episodes of about seven minutes each.

00:07:11.379 --> 00:07:16.020
It will feature mostly situational, nonverbal
comedy focusing on the life of the two characters

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:17.599
surviving in the big city.

00:07:17.599 --> 00:07:21.509
There's no set release date yet, but we do
know Chip 'n' Dale is coming at some point

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:22.629
in 2020.

00:07:22.629 --> 00:07:27.189
Until then, go watch the 1952 short "Pluto's
Christmas Tree" on Disney+ to see what these

00:07:27.189 --> 00:07:28.710
Chipmunks are all about.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.930
*chipmunk noises* *nut throw* *Pluto bark*

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:34.610
Star Wars: Jedi Temple Challenge

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:36.789
Remember Legends of the Hidden Temple and
Guts?

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:41.009
If you've got fond memories of those kid competition
shows, you might want to keep your eyes peeled

00:07:41.009 --> 00:07:43.139
for Star Wars: Jedi Temple Challenge.

00:07:43.139 --> 00:07:46.900
It's a live action skills-based game show
set in the Star Wars universe.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:51.039
It's also set to be hosted by Ahmed Best,
who portrayed Jar Jar Binks in the prequel

00:07:51.039 --> 00:07:52.039
trilogy.

00:07:52.039 --> 00:07:55.690
Jedi Temple Challenge will test contestants'
skills in three different settings: a forest

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:58.069
planet, a star cruiser, and a Jedi temple.

00:07:58.069 --> 00:08:01.960
According to Dan Silver, Vice President of
Disney Original Unscripted Content,

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:06.930
"Star Wars: Jedi Temple Challenge brings together
the best of Star Wars - competitive spirit,

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:11.800
harrowing obstacles and a hero's triumph over
challenges - in a totally new format for the

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:12.800
franchise."

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:16.479
It's a bit of an odd one, but Star Wars: Jedi
Temple Challenge could be pretty fun - it's

00:08:16.479 --> 00:08:20.780
hard to tell until the release gets closer,
and as of now, there's no concrete release

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.280
date other than some time in 2020.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:24.280
Stargirl

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.310
Based on Jerry Spinelli's novel of the same
name about nonconformity and romance in high

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:32.650
school, Stargirl is set to arrive on Disney+
on March 13, 2020.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:36.529
It's the story of high schooler Leo, who is
awestruck by a new student, Susan "Stargirl"

00:08:36.529 --> 00:08:37.529
Caraway.

00:08:37.529 --> 00:08:42.370
Stargirl is unique, interesting, and refuses
to conform to teen social norms, causing much

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.029
of the school to turn against her.

00:08:44.029 --> 00:08:45.870
Leo, however, falls in love with her.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:50.540
At Stargirl's center is the acting debut of
Grace VanderWaal, a 15-year-old singer-songwriter

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:53.570
who won America's Got Talent in 2016.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:57.959
VanderWaal had massive charisma and stage
presence during her run on America's Got Talent,

00:08:57.959 --> 00:08:59.940
so it'll be fun to see her in an acting role.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:03.810
As an added bonus, she'll be displaying her
singing and ukulele skills as well.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:04.810
Be Our Chef

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:09.120
The runaway popularity of cooking competition
shows in recent years has been hard to miss,

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.350
so it's no surprise that Disney+ has one on
the way in 2020.

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:17.029
Be Our Chef will feature two families competing
each week to create Disney-themed dishes that

00:09:17.029 --> 00:09:21.120
fit in the confines of that week's challenge,
with the winning team's final dish being turned

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.120
into a treat that will actually served at
Walt Disney World.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.770
"We invite you to relax.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:32.420
Let us pull up a chair as the dining room
proudly presents your dinner."

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:36.660
Be Our Chef is hosted by Angela Kinsey, who
is probably best known for playing Angela

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.510
on the U.S. version of The Office.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:42.730
Kinsey now hosts a YouTube cooking show with
her husband, Baking with Josh and Ange.

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:47.250
Further details about Be Our Chef, including
an exact premiere date, are yet to be announced,

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:51.070
but we can expect the competition to arrive
on Disney+ at some point this year.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.070
Short Circuit

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:53.720
No, this has nothing to do with Johnny-5.

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:57.870
Instead, Short Circuit sounds like it could
be a really fun way to discover new talent

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.339
in the animation world.

00:09:59.339 --> 00:10:04.399
Short Circuit is a short film project that
Disney began back in 2016, purportedly allowing

00:10:04.399 --> 00:10:08.699
anyone at Walt Disney Animation Studios the
chance to pitch their own ideas for potential

00:10:08.699 --> 00:10:11.221
production with the full support of the studio.

00:10:11.221 --> 00:10:15.550
The project opens the door for potentially
risky, unique, or offbeat stories that might

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.070
not otherwise have been told.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:21.310
14 different short films will debut with Short
Circuit's premiere on Disney+ at the end of

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:22.310
January.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:26.010
Disney has showed off a few of these films
at various expos and trade shows, like "Just

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:28.550
a Thought," "Exchange Student," and "Jing
Hua."

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:32.630
It looks like each film will vary wildly in
tone and animation style, and it might be

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:35.630
fun to see some undiscovered talent at Disney
work their magic.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:36.630
Lamp Life

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:40.690
If you saw Toy Story 4 and were confused about
how Bo Peep wound up where she did, "Lamp

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.120
Life" has got you covered.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:45.820
The story was originally conceived as a flashback
that would appear in the film, but it was

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:48.329
eventually cut for time and pacing issues.

00:10:48.329 --> 00:10:52.351
Instead, it's been reworked into the short
film "Lamp Life," premiering on Disney+ at

00:10:52.351 --> 00:10:53.351
the end of January.

00:10:53.351 --> 00:10:57.790
"Lamp Life" will reveal how Bo Peep made the
journey from Andy's family to Second Chance

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:58.790
Antiques.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:02.720
It will feature a few familiar voices from
the Toy Story films, including Annie Potts

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:07.680
as Bo Peep; Emily Davis as Billy, Goat, and
Gruff; and Ally Maki as Giggle McDimples.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:12.460
"Lamp Life" is directed by Valerie LaPoint,
who has directed a few other Pixar short films

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.330
and was a writer on Toy Story 4.

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:18.320
Choosing to release "Lamp Life" as its own
short film instead of an extra alongside Toy

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.970
Story 4 seems to indicate that it's been fleshed
out quite a bit.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:24.140
Pixar fans will definitely want to check it
out.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.140
Timmy Failure: Mistakes Were Made

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:28.830
Based on the Timmy Failure book series by
Stephan Pastis, Timmy Failure: Mistakes Were

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.040
Made is a film about a young boy who runs
a detective agency in Portland, Oregon.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:37.660
One day, Timmy's "Failuremobile," a Segway
his mother won in a contest, is stolen, and

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:40.000
Timmy sets out to crack the case with his
partner.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.950
By the way, Timmy's partner is an imaginary
1,500-pound polar bear.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:48.510
Judging from the trailer, Timmy Failure: Mistakes
Were Made looks like a fun cross between Encyclopedia

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:50.300
Brown and Calvin &amp; Hobbes.

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:53.880
Considering the source material, the film
could launch a whole family-friendly franchise

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:54.880
if it's successful.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:59.209
We'll find out how it goes - and hopefully,
who took the Segway - when it hits Disney+

00:11:59.209 --> 00:12:01.480
on February 7, 2020.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.540
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:07.899
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies and TV shows are coming soon.

00:12:07.899 --> 00:12:10.980
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

